From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zerollama <zerollama@local>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 01:33:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: add QJL/Polar/TBQ types, ops, and graph builders
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port type definitions and op infrastructure from elizaOS llama.cpp
fork for QJL (Quantized Johnson-Lindenstrauss), PolarQuant, and
TurboQuant KV-cache compression schemes.

Types added (ggml.h enum + ggml-common.h block structs):
  GGML_TYPE_TBQ3_0    (44) — 3-bit TurboQuant, QK=32
  GGML_TYPE_TBQ4_0    (45) — 4-bit TurboQuant, QK=32
  GGML_TYPE_QJL1_256  (46) — 1-bit JL-sketch K-cache (34 B/block)
  GGML_TYPE_Q4_POLAR  (47) — PolarQuant Q4 with optional QJL residual
  GGML_TYPE_TBQ3_TCQ  (48) — TCQ-3 trellis-coded TurboQuant (3.25 bpw)
  GGML_TYPE_TBQ3_K    (49) — TurboQuant 3-bit, QK_K layout
  GGML_TYPE_TBQ4_K    (50) — TurboQuant 4-bit, QK_K layout

Ops added:
  GGML_OP_ATTN_SCORE_QJL      — QJL packed-K attention score
  GGML_OP_ATTN_SCORE_TBQ      — TurboQuant packed-K attention score
  GGML_OP_ATTN_SCORE_POLAR    — PolarQuant packed-K attention score
  GGML_OP_FUSED_ATTN_QJL_TBQ  — fused QJL-K + TBQ-V attention

type_traits entries use blck_size/type_size only (no to_float/from_float
function pointers yet — those come with CPU kernels in the next patch).
Quantize switch cases are also deferred to 0027.

GGML_FTYPE_MOSTLY_Q4_POLAR = 102 added for GGUF model loading.
